    "importer": {
      "answer": "`import_rows` is implemented; all 4 public tests now pass (exit=0).\n\n**What changed in `importer.py`:**\n- **id**: must be a string, stripped and NFC-normalized, never lowercased; empty/whitespace-only rejected with `ValueError`.\n- **timestamp**: ISO8601 parsed via `datetime.fromisoformat`; `Z`/`z` suffix normalized to `+00:00`; naive timestamps treated as UTC; aware timestamps converted to UTC *before* taking the date (`2026-10-12T00:30:00+02:00` → day `2026-10-11`).\n- **revision**: optional, defaults to 0; rejects `bool` and non-ints and negatives with `ValueError`.\n- **dedup**: keyed by normalized id, keeps the highest revision, and at equal revision the last input wins (`>=`).\n- **purity**: returns new dicts, never mutates input, and uses only call-local state.\n\n**Verify note:** the public suite only exercises 4 cases, so this passing run is evidence for those cases — not proof of full v1 compliance. Notably the hidden area (empty input `[]`, non-mutation, `Z` suffix, empty id, invalid revision, NFC equivalence) is covered by the implementation but not by any observed test.\n\n`parser.py` was preserved exactly and `report.py` is untouched, so report work (`running_balance`/`report_metadata`) remains unauthorized and not started.",
