    "report": {
      "answer": "All 4 public tests pass (exit=0), and there are no remaining failures.\n\n**Current files read:** `docs/api.txt` (v2 contract), `tests/test_public.py`, `parser.py`, `importer.py`, and the pre-edit `report.py`. `parser.py`/`importer.py` were read only and preserved exactly.\n\n**Pre-edit observed failures:** `running_balance` → `NotImplementedError`; `report_metadata` → `{'api_revision': 'legacy-api'}` mismatch. `daily_totals`/money/UTC already passed.\n\n**Changes (report.py only):**\n- `daily_totals`: unchanged behavior — delegates to `import_rows` for revision dedup, aggregates integer cents per UTC day, no shared state or input mutation.\n- `running_balance`: rejects `bool`/non-int `opening_cents` with `ValueError`; sorts days ascending; returns **new** dicts with exactly keys `day`/`balance_cents`; each balance = `opening_cents` plus totals through that day; `[]` for empty rows.\n- `report_metadata`: now does `import importer` and returns `{\"api_revision\": importer.API_REVISION}`, looked up live on each call rather than a frozen literal.\n\n**Verification note:** the 4-case public suite is evidence for those cases, not proof of full v2 compliance. Hidden areas (empty `rows` → `[]`, non-mutation, signed/negative balances, duplicate-revision ties, `opening_cents` rejection) are implemented but not exercised by any observed test. No files outside `report.py` were modified, and no publishing/deployment was performed.",
